
MLOps Architecture – Suggested IAM Roles (Development + Staging/Production)

NOTE:
- These are logical roles and example names; you can adapt naming to your standards.
- Permissions should be scoped to specific ARNs (S3 buckets, ECR repos, KMS keys, RDS, etc.) instead of using wildcards in production.
- Many of these can be implemented as multiple roles if you want even finer separation of duties.

====================================================
1) DEVELOPMENT ACCOUNT – IAM ROLES
====================================================

1. Dev-SM-Studio-User-Role
   Used by: SageMaker Studio user profiles (Data Scientists / ML Engineers)
   Main permissions:
   - sagemaker:* (restricted to dev account resources where possible)
   - s3:GetObject, PutObject, ListBucket on:
     - dev training / evaluation / intermediate S3 buckets
   - ecr:GetAuthorizationToken, BatchGetImage, GetDownloadUrlForLayer on dev ECR repos
   - logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents on dev log groups
   - cloudwatch:GetMetricData, ListMetrics, GetMetricStatistics
   - kms:Encrypt, Decrypt, GenerateDataKey for specific KMS keys
   - secretsmanager:GetSecretValue or ssm:GetParameter for approved parameters
   - iam:PassRole for dev SageMaker execution roles only (if needed for pipelines)

2. Dev-SM-Training-Execution-Role
   Used by: SageMaker training / retraining pipelines and training jobs in Dev
   Main permissions:
   - sagemaker:CreateTrainingJob, CreateProcessingJob, CreateTransformJob, CreatePipelineExecution, Describe*, List*
   - s3:GetObject, PutObject, ListBucket on:
     - dev-ml-training-bucket
     - dev-ml-eval-bucket
   - ecr:GetAuthorizationToken, BatchGetImage, GetDownloadUrlForLayer on dev training images
   - logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents
   - cloudwatch:PutMetricData
   - kms:Encrypt, Decrypt, GenerateDataKey on training KMS keys
   - secretsmanager:GetSecretValue or ssm:GetParameter for training-related secrets
   - events:PutEvents (if pipeline needs to emit events)

3. Dev-SM-Inference-Execution-Role
   Used by: SageMaker inference pipelines in Dev (triggered by EventBridge / Lambda)
   Main permissions:
   - sagemaker:CreateProcessingJob, CreateTransformJob, CreateEndpoint*, InvokeEndpoint, Describe*, List*
   - s3:GetObject, PutObject, ListBucket on:
     - dev-ml-inference-input
     - dev-ml-inference-output
   - ecr:GetAuthorizationToken, BatchGetImage, GetDownloadUrlForLayer on inference images
   - logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents
   - cloudwatch:PutMetricData
   - kms:Encrypt, Decrypt, GenerateDataKey
   - secretsmanager:GetSecretValue or ssm:GetParameter for inference-related secrets

4. Dev-MLflow-Service-Role
   Used by: MLflow backend service (EC2/ECS/EKS/Lambda depending on implementation)
   Main permissions:
   - s3:GetObject, PutObject, ListBucket on dev-mlflow-artifacts bucket
   - s3:GetObject, ListBucket on training / inference buckets (to reference artifacts)
   - logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents for MLflow logs
   - kms:Encrypt, Decrypt if MLflow bucket or DB uses KMS
   - rds-db:connect (if MLflow tracking DB is in RDS)
   - secretsmanager:GetSecretValue or ssm:GetParameter for DB credentials

5. Dev-EventBridge-Invoke-SM-Role
   Used by: EventBridge rules that start SageMaker pipelines
   Main permissions:
   - sagemaker:StartPipelineExecution, CreateProcessingJob, CreateTransformJob on specific pipelines
   - iam:PassRole for Dev-SM-Inference-Execution-Role (if required)
   NOTE: This can also be the same as the pipeline execution role if preferred.

6. Dev-Lambda-Inference-Orchestrator-Role
   Used by: Lambda functions that orchestrate inference pipelines
   Main permissions:
   - lambda:Write logs (logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents)
   - sagemaker:StartPipelineExecution or CreateProcessingJob/TransformJob
   - s3:GetObject, PutObject on relevant input/output buckets
   - kms:Decrypt for reading encrypted data or secrets
   - secretsmanager:GetSecretValue or ssm:GetParameter

7. Dev-GitHub-Actions-Role
   Type: IAM role with OIDC trust to GitHub
   Used by: GitHub Actions workflows running from dev repo
   Main permissions:
   - ecr:CreateRepository, DescribeRepositories, InitiateLayerUpload, UploadLayerPart, CompleteLayerUpload, PutImage, BatchCheckLayerAvailability
   - s3:GetObject, PutObject, ListBucket on:
     - dev-cicd-artifacts bucket (if used)
   - sagemaker:UpdatePipeline, CreatePipeline, StartPipelineExecution (if CI/CD triggers pipelines)
   - iam:PassRole for Dev-SM-Training-Execution-Role / Dev-SM-Inference-Execution-Role (as needed)
   - logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents (optional for deployment logging)

8. Dev-ECR-Scan-Role (optional if using Aqua/other scanning service)
   Used by: Security tooling to scan dev ECR images
   Main permissions:
   - ecr:DescribeImages, ListImages, BatchGetImage
   - ecr:GetAuthorizationToken, GetDownloadUrlForLayer

9. Dev-DataCopy-From-Prod-Role (if data copy from Prod is automated)
   Used by: Cross-account data copy jobs (usually in Prod account assuming a pull model – but you may also have a dev-side role)
   Main permissions (dev side):
   - s3:PutObject on dev training buckets
   - kms:Encrypt with dev KMS keys
   Trust: Prod account service/role (if Prod is pushing data to Dev)

10. Dev-Secrets-Management-Role
    Used by: Automation that creates/rotates secrets for Dev
    Main permissions:
    - secretsmanager:CreateSecret, PutSecretValue, TagResource, DescribeSecret
    - kms:Encrypt, Decrypt for secrets KMS key

====================================================
2) STAGING / PRODUCTION ACCOUNT – IAM ROLES
====================================================

11. Prod-SM-Retraining-Execution-Role
    Used by: SageMaker retraining pipeline in retraining VPC
    Main permissions:
    - sagemaker:CreateTrainingJob, CreateProcessingJob, CreateTransformJob, CreatePipelineExecution, Describe*, List*
    - s3:GetObject, ListBucket on:
      - annotated data buckets
      - factory upload buckets (if needed)
    - s3:PutObject on:
      - retraining outputs bucket
    - ecr:GetAuthorizationToken, BatchGetImage, GetDownloadUrlForLayer on prod training images
    - logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents
    - cloudwatch:PutMetricData
    - kms:Encrypt, Decrypt for prod keys
    - secretsmanager:GetSecretValue or ssm:GetParameter (DB, endpoints, etc.)
    - mlflow: write/registry operations (if using fine-grained MLflow auth; otherwise covered by infra role)
    NOTE: This role must NOT have permissions to update production inference endpoints directly.

12. Prod-SM-Inference-Execution-Role
    Used by: SageMaker inference pipeline in inference VPC
    Main permissions:
    - sagemaker:CreateProcessingJob, CreateTransformJob, CreateEndpointConfig, CreateEndpoint, UpdateEndpoint, InvokeEndpoint, Describe*, List*
    - s3:GetObject on factory upload bucket (input)
    - s3:PutObject on inference output bucket (predictions, metadata)
    - ecr:GetAuthorizationToken, BatchGetImage, GetDownloadUrlForLayer on prod inference images
    - logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents
    - cloudwatch:PutMetricData (inference metrics)
    - kms:Encrypt, Decrypt, GenerateDataKey
    - secretsmanager:GetSecretValue or ssm:GetParameter for inference secrets
    - rds-db:connect (if pipeline writes inference metadata to RDS)

13. Prod-EventBridge-Invoke-SM-Role
    Used by: EventBridge rules that trigger retraining or inference pipeline
    Main permissions:
    - sagemaker:StartPipelineExecution or StartExecution on specific pipelines
    - iam:PassRole for Prod-SM-Retraining-Execution-Role / Prod-SM-Inference-Execution-Role (as required)

14. Prod-Lambda-Orchestration-Role
    Used by: Lambda functions that orchestrate production workflows (translation, QC, etc.)
    Main permissions:
    - lambda:Write logs (logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents)
    - sagemaker:StartPipelineExecution, CreateProcessingJob/TransformJob
    - s3:GetObject, PutObject, ListBucket on relevant production buckets (input, output, annotated)
    - rds:DescribeDBInstances, rds-db:connect (if Lambda talks to RDS)
    - kms:Decrypt / Encrypt
    - secretsmanager:GetSecretValue or ssm:GetParameter

15. Prod-CVAT-ECS-Task-Execution-Role
    Used by: ECS tasks running CVAT (Fargate/EC2)
    Main permissions:
    - ecr:GetAuthorizationToken, BatchGetImage, GetDownloadUrlForLayer (to pull CVAT image)
    - logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents for task logs
    - xray:PutTraceSegments, PutTelemetryRecords (if using X-Ray)

16. Prod-CVAT-ECS-Task-Role
    Used by: CVAT application containers
    Main permissions:
    - s3:GetObject, ListBucket on inference output bucket (to read images)
    - s3:PutObject on annotated data bucket
    - rds-db:connect to CVAT DB (Aurora/RDS)
    - kms:Decrypt for DB credentials and bucket encryption
    - secretsmanager:GetSecretValue or ssm:GetParameter for DB creds and app config
    - cloudwatch:PutMetricData (optional, if CVAT pushes custom metrics)

17. Prod-Grafana-Task-Role (if Grafana is deployed in ECS/EKS)
    Used by: Grafana container
    Main permissions:
    - cloudwatch:ListMetrics, GetMetricData, GetMetricStatistics
    - logs:DescribeLogGroups, DescribeLogStreams, GetLogEvents
    - secretsmanager:GetSecretValue or ssm:GetParameter for Grafana config

18. Prod-MLflow-Service-Role
    Used by: MLflow backend in production
    Main permissions:
    - s3:GetObject, PutObject, ListBucket on prod-mlflow-artifacts bucket
    - logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents
    - rds-db:connect to MLflow tracking DB
    - kms:Encrypt, Decrypt for artifacts and DB
    - secretsmanager:GetSecretValue or ssm:GetParameter for DB credentials
    - (Optional) sts:AssumeRole into Dev account for copying approved models / artifacts

19. Prod-GitHub-Actions-Deploy-Role
    Type: IAM role with OIDC trust to GitHub (separate from Dev)
    Used by: GitHub Actions workflows to deploy to Prod
    Main permissions:
    - ecr:BatchGetImage, GetDownloadUrlForLayer, PutImage, CreateRepository, DescribeRepositories
    - s3:GetObject, PutObject, ListBucket on:
      - prod deployment artifacts bucket
    - sagemaker:CreatePipeline, UpdatePipeline, StartPipelineExecution on prod pipelines
    - cloudformation:CreateStack, UpdateStack, DescribeStacks, DeleteStack (if using IaC for infra)
    - ecs:UpdateService, DescribeServices, RegisterTaskDefinition (for CVAT/Grafana ECS)
    - rds:ModifyDBInstance (if schema migrations are automated; or use a separate DB migration role)
    - iam:PassRole for:
      - Prod-SM-Retraining-Execution-Role
      - Prod-SM-Inference-Execution-Role
      - Prod-CVAT-ECS-Task-Execution-Role
    - logs:CreateLogGroup, CreateLogStream, PutLogEvents (optional)

20. Prod-ImageCopy-From-Dev-Role (Cross-account)
    Used by: GitHub Actions or automation to copy approved ECR images from Dev to Prod
    In Prod account:
      - ecr:CreateRepository, DescribeRepositories, BatchGetImage, PutImage
      - sts:AssumeRole to a Dev-side role that has ecr:BatchGetImage/GetDownloadUrlForLayer
    In Dev account (paired role):
      - ecr:BatchGetImage, GetDownloadUrlForLayer on approved repos
      - Trust: Prod account role

21. Prod-DataCopy-To-Dev-Role (if factory data is copied down for Dev training)
    Used by: Automation in Prod account
    Main permissions:
    - s3:GetObject, ListBucket on factory upload / annotated buckets
    - sts:AssumeRole to Dev-DataCopy-From-Prod-Role
    - kms:Decrypt for prod keys; kms:Encrypt for dev keys (through assumed role)

22. Prod-Secrets-Management-Role
    Used by: Automation managing production secrets
    Main permissions:
    - secretsmanager:CreateSecret, PutSecretValue, RotateSecret, DescribeSecret
    - kms:Encrypt, Decrypt for secrets KMS key

23. Global-Logging-and-Monitoring-Role (optional shared pattern in each account)
    Used by: Central monitoring/alerting solution (e.g., cross-account NewRelic/CloudWatch dashboards)
    Main permissions:
    - logs:DescribeLogGroups, DescribeLogStreams, GetLogEvents (read-only)
    - cloudwatch:ListMetrics, GetMetricData, GetMetricStatistics
    - xray:BatchGetTraces, GetServiceGraph (if enabled)

====================================================
3) IDENTITY / ACCESS PATTERNS
====================================================

A. Data Scientist / ML Engineer access (Dev)
   - Human users authenticate via SSO/Identity Center (or IAM users).
   - They assume Dev-DS-MLEngineer-Role which can:
     - Assume Dev-SM-Studio-User-Role (for Studio)
     - Read MLflow UI, CloudWatch logs and metrics
     - Read-only access to dev code repo (GitHub is usually separate, not IAM)

B. Annotator access (Prod – CVAT)
   - Annotators authenticate through Active Directory with MFA (Ping) via ALB.
   - IAM is mostly for backend services; ALB + AD + CVAT RBAC control human access.
   - No direct IAM roles for annotators are required beyond the ECS/CVAT task roles above.

C. Cloud Engineering / Platform Ops
   - Separate admin / ops roles with:
     - Full access to infra (VPC, networking, ECS, RDS, etc.)
     - Limited sagemaker:* where needed for support
     - Change management via IaC (CloudFormation/Terraform) and GitHub Actions.

This list gives you a practical starting set of IAM roles to implement the Dev + Staging/Prod MLOps architecture in your diagram. Each role should be backed by one or more customer-managed IAM policies that scope permissions down to only the ARNs actually required.
