## 1. DEVELOPMENT ACCOUNT ROLES
# -----------------------------------------------------
1. SageMakerStudioExecutionRole_Dev
   - For SageMaker Studio notebooks (data scientists & ML engineers)
   - Needs: s3 (dev buckets), sagemaker:*, ecr:*, logs, ssm/secrets, mlflow access

2. SageMakerPipelineExecutionRole_Dev
   - Used by ALL SageMaker Pipelines (training & inference) in Dev
   - Needs: s3 full on dev buckets, ecr, sagemaker:CreateTrainingJob/HyperParameterTuningJob/ProcessingJob, passrole, logs, events

3. SageMakerTrainingJobRole_Dev
   - Role assumed by training jobs (can be same as Pipeline role or separate)

4. LambdaInferenceTriggerRole_Dev
   - For Lambda that triggers inference pipeline on S3 upload (dev testing)
   - Needs: sagemaker:StartPipelineExecution, s3 read dev input bucket, logs

5. GitHubActions_Dev_ECR_Push_Role
   - Assumed by GitHub Actions OIDC to build & push Docker images to Dev ECR
   - Needs: ecr:*, ecr:GetAuthorizationToken (restricted to dev repo)

6. GitHubActions_Dev_SageMaker_Trigger_Role
   - Assumed by GitHub Actions to start SageMaker pipelines in Dev
   - Needs: sagemaker:StartPipelineExecution, passrole (to pipeline role)

7. MLflowServerRole_Dev (if MLflow is on EC2/ECS/EKS)
   - Access to S3 artifact bucket, DynamoDB (for tracking), logs

8. EventBridge_S3_Trigger_Role_Dev (optional)
   - For EventBridge → Lambda → SageMaker pipeline in dev

## 2. PRODUCTION ACCOUNT ROLES
# -----------------------------------------------------
9. SageMakerPipelineExecutionRole_Retraining_Prod
   - Used ONLY by retraining pipeline in the isolated Retraining VPC
   - Needs: s3 access to annotated data buckets, mlflow (prod), logs, NO auto model deploy permissions

10. SageMakerPipelineExecutionRole_Inference_Prod
    - Used by production inference pipeline in Inference VPC
    - Needs: s3 read factory input bucket, s3 write inference output bucket, RDS access, logs

11. LambdaInferenceOrchestratorRole_Prod
    - Lambda that gets triggered by S3 factory upload → starts inference pipeline
    - Needs: sagemaker:StartPipelineExecution (inference pipeline), s3 read, logs, RDS write

12. LambdaCVATConfigRole_Prod (if needed for CVAT updates)

13. ECS_CVAT_TaskRole_Prod
    - Role for CVAT ECS tasks (Fargate/EC2)
    - Needs: s3 read/write annotated & inference buckets, RDS/Aurora access, secrets manager (DB creds)

14. ECS_CVAT_ExecutionRole_Prod
    - ECS task execution role (logs, ecr pull, etc.)

15. GitHubActions_Prod_Deploy_Role
    - Assumed by GitHub Actions OIDC for production deployment
    - Critical role with manual approval gate
    - Permissions:
      - ecr: ReplicateImage (copy approved images from Dev → Prod ECR)
      - sagemaker:CreateModel, CreateEndpointConfig, CreateEndpoint (or Update), CreatePipeline, etc.
      - sagemaker:StartPipelineExecution (only retraining pipeline, NOT auto inference deploy)
      - ssm:PutParameter / ssm:GetParameter (for pipeline params)
      - PassRole to all production SageMaker/ECS roles above

16. GitHubActions_Prod_ECR_Copy_Role
    - Separate narrower role just for copying approved images Dev ECR → Prod ECR

17. MLflowServerRole_Prod (read-only for data scientists)

18. RDS_Inference_Metadata_Role_Prod
    - Used by inference pipeline to write inference logs/metadata to RDS/Aurora

## 3. CROSS-ACCOUNT ROLES (if Dev and Prod are separate AWS accounts)
# -----------------------------------------------------
19. CrossAccount_DevToProd_ECR_Replicate_Role (in Prod account)
    - Assumed by Dev account or GitHub Actions to replicate images

20. CrossAccount_Prod_MLflow_Copy_Role (if you copy models from Dev MLflow → Prod MLflow)

## 4. HUMAN ACCESS ROLES / MANAGED POLICIES
# -----------------------------------------------------
21. DataScientist_Dev_Access_Role
    - Assumed by data scientists via SSO or console
    - Full SageMaker Studio, MLflow write, S3 dev buckets, GitHub

22. DataScientist_Prod_Monitoring_Role
    - READ-ONLY access in Prod
    - CloudWatch, CloudWatch Logs, MLflow UI (read), NO S3 direct access, NO SageMaker create/update

23. ML_Engineer_Prod_Deploy_Role
    - For the very few people who can approve production deployments

24. Annotator_CVAT_Access (usually via Active Directory group → IAM role via SSO)
    - Only access to CVAT URL (via ALB + Ping MFA), no AWS console access

25. Security_Audit_Role
    - For security team to review ECR scans, CloudTrail, Config

## 5. SERVICE-LINKED ROLES (AWS auto-creates, just note)
# -----------------------------------------------------
- AWSServiceRoleForAmazonSageMakerNotebooks
- AWSServiceRoleForSageMaker
- AWSServiceRoleForECS (if using ECS)

# =====================================================
# RECOMMENDED NAMING CONVENTION
# -----------------------------------------------------
<Company>-<env>-<workload>-role
Examples:
MyCorp-dev-sagemaker-pipeline-role
MyCorp-prod-inference-pipeline-role
MyCorp-github-prod-deploy-role
MyCorp-datascientist-prod-monitoring-role

# =====================================================
# TRUST POLICIES SUMMARY
# -----------------------------------------------------
- SageMaker roles → trust: sagemaker.amazonaws.com
- Lambda roles      → trust: lambda.amazonaws.com
- ECS task roles    → trust: ecs-tasks.amazonaws.com
- GitHub Actions    → trust: OIDC token from your GitHub repo/org
  (sts:AssumeRoleWithWebIdentity + conditions on repo & branch)

